FILE pair-1/A/PROJECT.md 
 # Staff training desk

Private application for an internal training coordinator and employee portal. Target runtime is Node 22 ESM. There are no runtime dependencies. Use `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, and `npm test` after installing the declared development tooling.

`model.ts` owns directory email normalization and domain error codes. `store.ts` owns per-desk mutable session state. `desk.ts` is the trusted in-process application API. `portal.ts` contains the current JSON submission caller and attendance export caller. Seeds come from the coordinator's typed configuration, not arbitrary JSON; their business constraints are checked at desk construction. Submission JSON is untrusted and is validated at the portal boundary. Unknown extra JSON fields are ignored today.

Employees enroll in a session with a fixed positive seat capacity. Emails are trimmed and lowercased, then checked for a basic email shape. Duplicate enrollment is rejected. Cancellation removes an existing enrollment. Attendance contains confirmed employees in enrollment order.

Enrollment accepts optional `{ waitlist: boolean }`: free seats are confirmed, and full sessions accept opt-ins onto a FIFO waiting list. Rosters include confirmed, waitlisted and offered statuses. Offers reserve seats but are excluded from attendance. Cancelling a confirmed employee offers a seat to the earliest waiting employee while admissions are open. `setAdmissions(sessionId, open)` pauses or resumes admissions; sessions start open and rosters expose `admissionsOpen`. Paused sessions reject all enrollment requests with ADMISSIONS_CLOSED before email or duplicate checks. Cancellation stays available during a pause without making offers. Reopening offers every available seat to the waiting list before new arrivals can enroll. Repeating an admissions state is harmless.

Domain failures throw `DeskError` with stable `code` values: INVALID_SESSION, DUPLICATE_SESSION, NOT_FOUND, INVALID_EMAIL, ALREADY_ENROLLED, FULL, NOT_ENROLLED, NOT_OFFERED, ADMISSIONS_CLOSED. Portal submission translates domain errors into failure replies; malformed JSON shapes, including a present nonboolean `waitlist`, produce BAD_REQUEST. Unexpected programming errors propagate. For desk operations, session existence is checked before email validation. Failed operations do not change state. Each desk owns its data; seeds, returned enrollments, rosters and attendance arrays may be mutated by callers without altering stored data.

The desk and portal exports are used only by this application and its tests; there are no external package consumers. Tests execute built JavaScript from dist. Keep the attendance export and portal submission consistent with the application rules.

`acceptOffer(sessionId, email)` confirms an offered entry, even while admissions are paused, and returns a detached enrollment. `declineOffer(sessionId, email)` removes an offered entry. Both check session existence before normalizing email, then require an existing offered entry (NOT_ENROLLED or NOT_OFFERED otherwise). Declining or cancelling an offer releases its seat; the next waiter receives an offer only when admissions are open. Offers do not expire.


